"Register D24-D32 and wire the workbook branch, additively over `register_skeleton`.\n\n    Called by `build_curriculum_factory_graph` immediately after `register_\n    unit_repair_topology` (N90 finding F2): `binding_inventory()` and\n    `unit_repair_binding_inventory()` both still deliberately exclude D24-D32\n    (their own docstrings document why -- `register_skeleton`/`unit_graph\n    .register_unit_path` must never see them directly), but\n    `full_binding_inventory()` widens further to include\n    `workbook.WORKBOOK_NODE_BODIES`, and this function is the one production\n    compile point's own step that turns that widened set into real,\n    `add_node`-registered nodes with real outgoing edges.\n    `register_skeleton` itself must never see these bindings; this function\n    adds exactly the nodes `register_skeleton` did not, then wires them over\n    the *full* merged node set so `workbook.register_workbook_path` can\n    resolve `D90`/`D91`/`D98`/M07/M08 as real, already-registered targets.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    workbook_bindings = dict(workbook.WORKBOOK_NODE_BODIES)\n    validate_bindings(workbook_bindings, required=tuple(workbook_bindings))","numLines":20,"startLine":536,"totalLines":666}}}
